WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.085
In the vision Mamba layer, the input first passes through a layer normalization module.

2
00:00:06.085 --> 00:00:09.578
The normalized features enter the SS2D Block.

3
00:00:09.578 --> 00:00:14.181
The block output is combined with a residual skip connection.

4
00:00:14.181 --> 00:00:18.415
The signal then undergoes a second layer normalization step.

5
00:00:18.415 --> 00:00:22.278
Next, it is processed by a feed-forward network.

6
00:00:22.278 --> 00:00:27.622
A final addition node merges the feed-forward output with its shortcut connection.

7
00:00:27.622 --> 00:00:32.967
Looking inside the SS2D block, the input starts at a linear layer.

8
00:00:32.967 --> 00:00:36.459
It continues through a depthwise convolution layer.

9
00:00:36.459 --> 00:00:39.581
A SiLU activation function is applied.

10
00:00:39.581 --> 00:00:43.815
The activations then pass into the core SS2D operation.

11
00:00:43.815 --> 00:00:46.937
This is followed by layer normalization.

12
00:00:46.937 --> 00:00:52.652
A top linear layer projects the intermediate features to the final block output.

13
00:00:52.652 --> 00:00:58.737
In the original state space model, the bottom step computes the recurrent state update.

14
00:00:58.737 --> 00:01:04.081
The top step maps the updated state to produce the recurrent output.

15
00:01:04.081 --> 00:01:07.944
This architecture is modified to integrate Mamba adapters.

16
00:01:07.944 --> 00:01:11.807
Processing begins with the initial state space update.

17
00:01:11.807 --> 00:01:14.930
The intermediate representation passes through Adaptor-T.

18
00:01:14.930 --> 00:01:18.793
It flows into the state space output computation.

19
00:01:18.793 --> 00:01:23.396
Finally, Adaptor-S completes the module to generate the adapted output.

